From: sixtyeightk <sixtyeightk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:57:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Full-screen (tall) output, batched planes for Arcus,
 lag diagnostic

- Native tall planes: 32 KB VRAM above 64 KB (VDP command A16), 128x64 planes the host marks
  tall; tall_written tracks which memory each map plane's name table was last written in
  (whole-table rewrites switch back, overlays are mirrored into the tall plane).
- gvdp_set_tall / gvdp_set_tall_planes / gvdp_render_scanline_ex: fixed output height with
  extra rows above and below the raster, the bottom window band moved to the last rows,
  sprite masking ignored and sprites cleared under the moved window; letterboxed otherwise.
- genesis_switch_docked(); VRAM dumps append tall VRAM, VSRAM, registers and tall state.
- GENESIS_LAG_ADDR dev lag-frame counter; input scripts up to 16384 directives.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EUc3W7pjjt53fhDNSnaeF9
